{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y1`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only observed data variable scored by a sampling statement is the top-level data variable `y1`, which is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. `x1`, `x2`, and `N` are context inputs and are not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  vector[N] x1; // Complete observation
  vector[N] y1; // Complete observation
  vector[N] x2; // Incomplete observation
}

parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

model {
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  y1 ~ normal(x1, sigma);
}

generated quantities {
  // Predict completion of second observation using
  // conditional variate model from first observation
  array[N] real y2_pred = normal_rng(x2, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":1,"x1":[4.164660011199408],"x2":[6.211113122187613],"y1":[3.557793173295816]}","protected_variables":["y1"]}
